task: agents-origin-rule
agent: opus5-bench
started: 2026-09-08
branch: feature/agents-origin-rule
worktree: ../okay-wt-originrule

why: operator instruction 2026-09-08, after `git push origin master`
  took origin from b6063224 to eca8877e (60 commits, fast-forward).
  AGENTS.md says `origin/master` is "STALE BY DESIGN — it is days
  behind, because nothing here pushes" and that there is "no remote
  sync step". Both were true this morning and are false now, and a
  coordination rule that misdescribes the world is worse than none:
  the next agent reads it and treats a current origin as garbage.

what: correct the two places that assert origin is stale, WITHOUT
  weakening the prohibition they justify. The rule "never reset or
  merge to origin/*" must stand on its own feet: origin is not
  guaranteed current at any moment (it is current only just after
  someone pushes), so `merge --ff-only origin/master` still discards
  every lane landed since the last push. The 2026-09-03 incident
  stays as the evidence it is.

predict: a paragraph edit, no code. The gate runs anyway because the
  rule says so, not because markdown can break it.
